    id: "econ-2021-ol-q11-b-i-pos", topicId: "economics-4-1", conceptId: "advantages-of-globalisation",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2021 OL Q11(b)(i) — advantage",
    questionText: "Outline one advantage or one disadvantage of globalisation. Indicate which one you are answering by placing a tick (✓) in the box below: Answer for: ADVANTAGE.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"bestNofParts","notation":"1 @ 5","answer":1,"ofParts":8,"perPart":5}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "An advantage of globalisation — any one", marks: 5, contextNote: "One advantage, 5 marks. The paper asks for an advantage OR a disadvantage, ticked; the scheme lists both, so each is its own route.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":5,"options":["Employment: MNCs provide jobs and skills particularly in exporting where large workforces are required.","Advancements of ICT: MNCs bring new technology with them as they set up in countries","Economic growth in developing countries: Much scope for developing countries to benefit from globalisation - creates employment and a higher standard of living for people living in these areas.","Spin-off effects: Global companies infuse wealth and foreign currency into local economies - this is used to purchase local resources and raw materials generating further revenue for local businesses and governments.","Boosts competition: Globalisation boosts ongoing competition between countries all over the world - lower prices for consumers.","Improvements in fair trade: Globalisation has greatly reduced trade barriers between countries through adjustment of tariffs and import duties.","New experiences: Globalisation exposes us to new ideas, experiences, lifestyles and cultures - closer relationships between countries.","Improved government relations: Helps bring different governments together so that they can work together towards achieving common goals."]} },
    ],
