    section: "B", questionRef: "2023 OL Q11(c)(ii)",
    stem: "The hidden economy in the hair & beauty market is estimated to be worth €400m. The Irish government is concerned about the size of this hidden economy.",
    questionText: "Outline one effect the hidden economy in the hair and beauty industry has on businesses in this industry and on the Irish government.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal","notation":"10","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-business", kind: "point", verbatim: "Loss of income to the firms that are in the legitimate economy that pay all their taxes.\n\nLegitimate firms may be forced to cut their prices / alter their standard of service.\n\nPossible exploitation of workers: they may not be paid the minimum wage.\n\nPossible closure of legitimate businesses.\n\nThere is a skills shortage in the legitimate hair and beauty sector which has a negative impact on the services that can be provided.", marks: null, contextNote: "One effect on businesses in this industry. Complete BOTH headings. The scheme prices the two together as one 10: the first correct effect 6 marks and the second 4, with no fixed share for either.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-government", kind: "point", verbatim: "Loss of revenue to the state in unpaid taxes.\n\nAdditional costs to the state of monitoring the hidden economy.\n\nMay lead to increased crime e.g. in the supply of illegal drugs.\n\nReputational damage to the country as it may be seen as a haven for tax evasion.", marks: null, contextNote: "One effect on the Irish government. An effect on the state.", openList: true },
    ],
