    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, Economics 2023 Ordinary Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "econ-2023-ol-q14-a-ii-reason", topicId: "economics-3-3", conceptId: "petrol-price-rise-cause-and-consumer-effect",
    section: "B", questionRef: "2023 OL Q14(a)(ii)",
    stem: "The line graph below shows changes in the price of petrol in Ireland from April to September 2022.",
    questionText: "Outline one reason why the price of petrol changed from April to June in the line graph above and explain one effect this had on Irish consumers.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal","notation":"12","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 12,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-reason", kind: "point", verbatim: "The easing of restrictions following lockdowns lead to an increase in demand for petrol as people were able to move more freely around the country and businesses were back to normal.\n\nHowever, the sharp increase in price later in the year was brought about by the EU sanctions imposed on Russian oil following the invasion of Ukraine. The lack of supply caused the sharp increase in price until alternative sources of oil were found.", marks: null, contextNote: "One reason the price changed. Give a reason AND an effect. The scheme prices the two together as one 12: the first correct answer 8 marks and the second 4, with no fixed share for either.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-effect", kind: "point", verbatim: "The increase in petrol prices leads to consumers having a lower standard of living as the cost of living increases. An increase in the price of petrol inevitably leads to an increase in the cost of producing and transporting goods. Some consumers reduced the number of journeys undertaken. Some consumers switched to use more public transport or walk or cycle where possible or switch to EVs.", marks: null, contextNote: "One effect on Irish consumers. Explain the effect on consumers.", openList: true },
    ],
