          "alt": "The printed question as the paper sets it. A demand and supply diagram of Irish farm output. Price on the vertical axis, Quantity on the horizontal. A red downward-sloping line labelled D crosses a blue upward-sloping line labelled S at a filled dot labelled E, with grey guides to Pe on the price axis and Qe on the quantity axis. Beneath it the note that the price of fertiliser in Ireland increased by 97.7% in the 12 months to October 2022, and the parts asking the student to show the effect on the diagram, explain it, and explain the term substitute good. The printed text reads: (b) The diagram below shows the demand and supply curve for Irish farm output. The price of fertiliser in Ireland increased by 97.7% in the 12 months to October 2022. Adapted from the CSO (i) As a result, the increase in fertiliser prices has affected the supply of Irish farm output. Show the effect of this development on the diagram above. (ii) Explain your answer. Price Quantity E D S Pe Qe",
